E('sigmund freud|freud|psychoanalysis', 'Sigmund Freud was an Austrian neurologist who founded psychoanalysis.', 'He lived from 1856 to 1939.', 'He believed unconscious desires shape behaviour.', 'He wrote The Interpretation of Dreams in 1899.', 'He described the id, ego and superego.', 'Many of his theories are now disputed, but his influence is huge.', 'He fled Nazi-occupied Vienna to London in 1938.')
E('carl jung|jung', 'Carl Jung was a Swiss psychiatrist who founded analytical psychology.', 'He lived from 1875 to 1961.', 'He was an early colleague of Freud before they split.', 'He described the “collective unconscious” and archetypes.', 'He introduced the ideas of introversion and extraversion.')
E('ivan pavlov|pavlov', 'Ivan Pavlov was a Russian physiologist famous for his experiments with dogs.', 'He lived from 1849 to 1936.', 'He showed dogs could learn to salivate at a signal linked to food.', 'This is called classical conditioning.', 'He won the Nobel Prize in 1904 for work on digestion.')
E('john maynard keynes|keynes', 'John Maynard Keynes was an influential British economist.', 'He lived from 1883 to 1946.', 'He argued governments should spend more during recessions.', 'His ideas shaped economic policy after the Great Depression.', 'He helped design the post-war Bretton Woods system.')
E('mary shelley|frankenstein', 'Mary Shelley was an English writer, author of Frankenstein.', 'She lived from 1797 to 1851; Frankenstein was published in 1818.', 'She began it at 18 during a ghost-story contest with Lord Byron.', 'It is often called the first science-fiction novel.', 'Her mother was the feminist writer Mary Wollstonecraft.')
E('lord byron|byron', 'Lord Byron was an English Romantic poet.', 'He lived from 1788 to 1824.', 'His works include Don Juan.', 'He was famous for scandal and was called “mad, bad and dangerous to know”.', 'He died while supporting Greek independence.', 'His daughter was Ada Lovelace.')
E('h g wells|the time machine|war of the worlds', 'H. G. Wells was an English writer and a pioneer of science fiction.', 'He lived from 1866 to 1946.', 'He wrote The Time Machine and The War of the Worlds.', 'A 1938 radio version of The War of the Worlds reportedly caused some panic.', 'He imagined tanks and atomic bombs before they existed.')
E('jules verne', 'Jules Verne was a French novelist and a father of science fiction.', 'He lived from 1828 to 1905.', 'He wrote Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Sea and Around the World in Eighty Days.', 'He imagined submarines and moon journeys.', 'He is one of the most translated authors ever.')
E('homer greek poet|sappho', 'Sappho was an ancient Greek poet from the island of Lesbos.', 'She lived around 630 to 570 BC.', 'She wrote lyric poetry about love.', 'Only fragments of her work survive.', 'Plato reportedly called her “the tenth Muse”.')
E('confucius sayings|analects', 'The Analects is a collection of sayings of Confucius.', 'It was compiled by his followers after his death in 479 BC.', 'It covers virtue, learning and government.', 'A famous line: “Learning without thought is labour lost.”')
E('abacus', 'The abacus is a counting tool using beads on rods.', 'Early forms were used in Mesopotamia; the bead abacus spread in China by the 2nd century BC.', 'It helped merchants calculate quickly.', 'It is still used to teach arithmetic in some countries.')
E('zero|number zero|history of zero', 'Zero as a number was developed in India.', 'The mathematician Brahmagupta set out rules for zero around AD 628.', 'The Babylonians and Maya used zero-like placeholders earlier.', 'It reached Europe through Arabic mathematicians.', 'It made modern mathematics possible.')
E('money history|first coins|history of money', 'Money developed to make trade easier.', 'The first coins were made in Lydia, in modern Turkey, around 600 BC.', 'Before coins, people bartered or used items like shells.', 'China introduced paper money around the 11th century.', 'Today most money exists digitally.')
E('glass|history of glass', 'Glass has been made by people for thousands of years.', 'The first glass objects appeared in Mesopotamia around 2500 BC.', 'Glassblowing was invented around the 1st century BC.', 'Venice became famous for glassmaking.', 'Glass lenses led to spectacles, telescopes and microscopes.')
E('chocolate history|cacao', 'Chocolate comes from the seeds of the cacao tree in the Americas.', 'Mesoamericans drank chocolate thousands of years ago.', 'The Aztecs used cacao beans as money.', 'Spain brought it to Europe in the 16th century.', 'Solid chocolate bars appeared in the 19th century.')
E('tea history|history of tea', 'Tea has been drunk in China for thousands of years.', 'Legend says Emperor Shennong discovered it around 2737 BC.', 'It spread to Japan and Korea.', 'It became hugely popular in Britain from the 17th century.', 'Tea taxes helped spark the Boston Tea Party.')
E('coffee history|history of coffee', 'Coffee originated in Ethiopia.', 'Coffee drinking spread in Yemen in the 15th century.', 'Coffee houses spread through the Ottoman Empire and Europe.', 'London coffee houses became centres of business and news.', 'Lloyd’s of London began in a coffee house.')
E('nobel peace prize|peace prize', 'The Nobel Peace Prize honours work for peace.', 'It was first awarded in 1901.', 'It is awarded in Oslo, Norway.', 'Winners include Martin Luther King Jr., Nelson Mandela and Malala Yousafzai.', 'Gandhi never won it.')
E('red cross|henry dunant', 'The Red Cross is a humanitarian movement that helps people in war and disaster.', 'It was founded in 1863.', 'Henry Dunant was inspired after seeing the wounded at the Battle of Solferino.', 'The Geneva Conventions protect wounded soldiers and civilians.', 'Dunant shared the first Nobel Peace Prize in 1901.')
E('geneva conventions', 'The Geneva Conventions are treaties setting rules for war.', 'The first was adopted in 1864; the main modern ones date from 1949.', 'They protect wounded soldiers, prisoners and civilians.', 'Nearly every country has signed them.')
E('olympus mons mythology|underworld|hades', 'Hades was the Greek god of the underworld.', 'His stories come from ancient Greek myth.', 'He was a brother of Zeus and Poseidon.', 'He ruled the dead with his wife, Persephone.', 'The three-headed dog Cerberus guarded his realm.')
E('poseidon', 'Poseidon was the Greek god of the sea, earthquakes and horses.', 'He was worshipped across ancient Greece.', 'He carried a three-pronged trident.', 'He was a brother of Zeus.', 'The Romans called him Neptune.')
E('athena', 'Athena was the Greek goddess of wisdom and war strategy.', 'She was the patron goddess of Athens.', 'She was born fully armed from Zeus’s head.', 'Her symbol was the owl.', 'The Parthenon was her temple.')
E('apollo god', 'Apollo was the Greek god of the sun, music, poetry and prophecy.', 'He was one of the twelve Olympians.', 'His oracle at Delphi was the most famous in Greece.', 'He was twin brother of Artemis.', 'NASA named its Moon program after him.')
